From 2f129011e8d1e5db3f846b62b486495a0682bd0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:25:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] swscale arm: scaling to RGB32 in NEON (fast bilinear,
 yuv2rgbx32)

With SWS_FAST_BILINEAR to RGB32/BGR32 (RGBA/BGRA on little-endian) the
32-bit ARM path was C: the fast bilinear horizontal scalers and the
packed RGB output. Now, bit-exact with the C:
 - ff_hyscale_fast/ff_hcscale_fast: 8 outputs a step, the positions and
   weights in NEON and the source bytes through vtbl, for scales down to
   about 1.85x (the rest of the line, and larger scales, in C);
 - yuv2rgbx32 _1 and _2: the 32 bpp tables as arithmetic,
   clip((Y * cy + k + ((clip(C) * c) >> 16) * cy) >> 16) per channel,
   which ff_yuv2rgb_c_init_tables now also stores
   (SwsContext.yuv2rgb_arith, _ok where it applies and fits 32 bits).
Byte-element loads and stores only.
